# Unused Exports

Which exported symbols in `src/` are never imported anywhere in this
repo. Ground truth via ts-morph (a real TypeScript compiler API
resolver, not regex): resolves barrel re-exports, renamed imports,
type-only usage, and usage that only appears under `tests/`, none of
which a grep-based approach gets right by construction.

## Policy grant this example needs

`.livestage/policy.json` in this directory: `code.languages` includes
`javascript`, nothing else. `@code` can reach for any npm package the
project already has as a devDependency (ts-morph here), the same policy
surface as `examples/database/`'s driver script.

## Result

@code language="javascript" src="unused-exports.js" label="dead" visible="false" cache="persist" cache-key="../../src/**/*.ts" /

**{{ dead.count }}** exported symbol(s) in `src/` are never imported
anywhere else in this repo. The script emits structured data only, no
pre-formatted markdown: `@render source=` binds the array directly.

@render source="dead.items" type="table" columns="symbol,file,kind,reExportedThroughBarrel" /

## Re-exported through a barrel

Every dead symbol whose barrel-reachability still matters (it's exposed
by more than its own declaring file, so deleting it means checking the
barrel too), via `@foreach`'s `where=` over the same bound array, no
second script run, no second policy grant:

@foreach item in {{ dead.items }} where="reExportedThroughBarrel == true"
- {{ item.symbol }} in {{ item.file }}
@foreach-end
